  "behavior": [
    "Trusted library sample_git_scoped takes a registered root and explicit QualifiedLocator. Component-relative native handles reject links, nested repositories and scope-external Git dependencies before subprocess dispatch.",
    "Captured ordinary worktree and scope-internal Git metadata/attributes/object dependencies supply an exclusive private view. Fixed supported commands do not reopen source bodies. Cumulative input/entry/time/cancellation budgets cover capture and source revalidation.",
    "Native source identity, length and high-precision version checks reject in-place modification; final root-route checks reject renamed roots and replaced ancestors. Unix size/version come from the same metadata observation. Windows native handle enumeration is implemented but awaits D36 native execution.",
    "Private capture preserves executable mode and modification observations. The supported fixed status command retains final private version verification and explicit cleanup. Arbitrary git diff commands are not a supported readonly contract.",
    "The macOS hydration policy is entered before source capture and restored on success/error; actual cloud-provider no-download acceptance remains open. No remote collector command, durable job or dangerous write capability was enabled."
  ],
